      "problem": "Which of the following is congruent to $0$ modulo $16?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, recall that \n\n$$\na≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a=kn,\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in Z.$ In other words, when $a$ is divided by $n,$ there is no remainder. This means that any integer multiple of $16$ is congruent to $0$ modulo $16.$ \n\nTherefore, since $16\\,|\\,64,$ we obtain \n\n$$\n64≡4\\cdot 16≡4\\cdot 0≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,16).\n$$\n\nNone of the other options are multiples of $16.$",
